@[systemd page]
After @[enchantment install init systemd], the new system boots with systemd.
Some things work differently from simpleinit-msb:

Services: @[systemctl enable --now sshd] (instead of telinit enable);
  @[systemctl status sshd], @[systemctl list-units --failed]. The init.d
  scripts are still installed (the smgl-system spell needs them), but unused.
Logins: a getty runs on tty1, and on tty2..6 once you switch to them.
  Logins are registered with logind (@[loginctl]), which gives users their
  seat's devices and a @[systemctl --user] instance.
Logs: in the journal (@[journalctl -b], @[journalctl -u sshd]). metalog stays
  installed but has no unit; @[dispel metalog] if you don't want it.
Network: systemd-networkd and systemd-resolved are enabled. For a wired
  connection with DHCP, write /etc/systemd/network/20-wired.network:
    [Match]
    Name=en*
    [Network]
    DHCP=yes
  and let resolved handle DNS:
  @[ln -sf ../run/systemd/resolve/stub-resolv.conf /etc/resolv.conf]
  Wifi: wpa_supplicant (in the base system) has no unit; write
  /etc/systemd/system/wpa_supplicant@.service with
    [Unit]
    BindsTo=sys-subsystem-net-devices-%i.device
    After=sys-subsystem-net-devices-%i.device
    [Service]
    ExecStart=/sbin/wpa_supplicant -c /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf -i %i
    [Install]
    WantedBy=multi-user.target
  then @[systemctl enable wpa_supplicant@wlan0] (your interface name, see
  @[ip link]) and a .network like the one above with Name=wl*. Do this
  before rebooting (in @[enchantment chroot]) on a machine without a cable.
Time: systemd-timesyncd keeps the clock in sync (@[timedatectl]).
Hostname, locale, keymap: @[hostnamectl], @[localectl] (after first boot).
Console font: FONT= in /etc/vconsole.conf (none: the kernel's font, which
is 16x32 on large screens or with fbcon=font:TER16x32); e.g.
FONT=latarcyrheb-sun32 (fonts in /usr/share/consolefonts).

To see this again, type @[todo systemd].
